>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `clear_rules`

``` hol4
simpLib.clear_rules : simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes all rules from a simpset, keeping its settings.

`clear_rules ss` removes the rewrites, conversions, congruence rules,
decision procedures, loopers and fragments of `ss`. It keeps the rewrite
maker, limit, solvers, subgoaler, side-condition depth and term order.
Thus `SIMP_TAC (clear_rules ss) ths` simplifies with `ths` alone, under
the settings of `ss`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>+ SIMP_CONV (simpLib.clear_rules bool_ss) [] “p ∧ T”;
>> SIMP_CONV (simpLib.clear_rules bool_ss) [AND_CLAUSES] “p ∧ T”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.filter_rewrites`](#simpLib.filter_rewrites),
[`simpLib.remove_ssfrags`](#simpLib.remove_ssfrags).
